      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "The integrand has the shape of an inverse trigonometric derivative, \\( \\frac{d}{dx} \\arcsin\\left(\\frac{x + 3}{2}\\right) = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4 - \\left(x + 3\\right)^{2}}} \\).",
         "rule_named": "antiderivative read from a derivative rule"
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "With \\( u = \\frac{x + 3}{2}, \\; dx = 2\\,du \\), the integral becomes \\( \\int \\frac{11}{2\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}} \\cdot 2\\,du = 11 \\int \\frac{du}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}} \\), which is \\( 11 \\arcsin{\\left(\\frac{x}{2} + \\frac{3}{2} \\right)} + C \\).",
